# A Pythonic Object
object representations:
- repr() string representation of object for developer, str() for user -- implement __repr__ and __str__ methods in your objects to support these

@classmethod decorator -- to define a method that operates on the class and not on instances, changes the way the method is called, so it receives *cls* and not *self* as a first argument -- good for alternative constructors

@staticmethod -- modifies method so that it doesn't receive special first arg -- like defining a plain function in class body -- not much used though

__format__ can be used to create custom .format() on object 
__hash__ (should return hash) and __eq__ need to be implemented to make object hashable
@property decorator -- make method read-only
- name mangling -- no private attributes in python, but you can do names like __method to hide them but its just about obscurity not security

-- overriding class attributes -- best way is to create a subclass
